## Grounding: index before code

**Two jobs, never confused.** The **code graph** is the authority for what exists and its exact signature; the
**docs** explain how a thing is meant to be used. Order on any unfamiliar surface: **docs to understand, code to
confirm, then write.** A method name seen in prose is never confirmation. **No code that calls a library is written
before that library is in a graph** — declare + install → build/refresh the graph → write the grounded call.

| Lane | Path | Authority for |
|---|---|---|
| `engine` | `{{ENGINE_LANE_PATH}}` | the installed `rag_wright` package — every `rag_wright.api` call grounds here first |
| `project` | `{{PROJECT_LANE_PATH}}` | this product's own code + libraries |

The **`using-the-rag-wright-engine`** skill is the engine-usage playbook: how to install, build these lanes, ground
every engine call, and follow the build sequence. Load it before engine work.

